 "definition": "E7-G (E7 registration amendment 6, results/e7/prediction.json): a same-GPU-family reference for E7's toggles.\nThe production toggles ran on V100 and their reference row (Arm T, wd 0.0034, seeds 20-22) on P100. E7-G reruns that\nreference row unchanged (code/e7_grid.py row T_wd0.0034, frozen vit_jepa.py, 50 epochs, seeds 20-22, three runs packed\non one GPU as the toggles were) on a V100, and scores it with the frozen per-run scorer (code/e7_score.py score_run).\nReading (fixed before the run):\n  gpu_check   per seed and seed-mean, the V100 reference's measured count at the last horizon minus the P100 one (and at\n              epoch 20). |seed-mean difference| <= 2 sd (3.16, the registered toggle threshold: 2 x the C5 reference\n              row's seed sd of the race's error, score.json toggles.*.sd_ref_headroom_error) -> 'no GPU-family difference\n              beyond 2 sd detectable at 3 seeds' (amendment 7: wording only; low power, not 'same count'); otherwise\n              'GPU-family sensitivity' and the toggles are read against the V100 row. Amendment 7 also reports the\n              paired per-seed differences with their mean, sd and t interval (2 df) at both horizons.\n  toggles_v100  the registered toggle statistic (e7_score.toggles: mean over seeds of toggle error - reference error,\n              headroom_200 and early_200, last horizon) recomputed with the V100 rows as the reference, read with the\n              registered threshold 3.16 and the registered directions; reported beside the registered (P100) reading.\nScope: the comparison is hardware plus packing and run-to-run nondeterminism, on shared seeds 20-22 (the P100 runs were\npacked with other rows' runs, the V100 runs with each other). Per run: GPU name, memory, driver, node (as an md5 prefix; names are redacted), torch, the pip\nfreeze hash and its agreement with results/e3/cluster_env.json, code commit and seed.\nNo registered verdict is re-scored.\nUsage: python3 code/e7g.py sbatch DIR COMMIT | score RUNS_DIR DATA_DIR PROD_ROWS.json PROD_SCORE.json OUT.json",
